<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	LOCAL FORK: upstream declares `aps-environment` (push notifications) and
	`com.apple.developer.networking.wifi-info` (current SSID) here. Neither is
	referenced anywhere in this codebase -- there is no
	registerForRemoteNotifications and no CNCopyCurrentNetworkInfo /
	NEHotspotNetwork call.

	Both are removed because a free Apple ID ("personal team") cannot be granted
	either capability. Leaving them in makes signing fail outright with
	"Provisioning profile doesn't include the ... entitlement" -- a confusing
	error for a capability the app never uses.

	Restore them only alongside a paid Developer Program account AND code that
	actually needs them.
	-->
</dict>
</plist>
